    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d416">

                <pb facs="0530" n="516" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg516"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 PW (Peace)/8–2947: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Political Adviser in
                        Korea</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jacobs</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-09-11T12:00:00-04:00">September 11,
                            1947—noon</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>191. Inf CinCFE. Urtel 306, Aug 29. Inform Kimm Kiusic message being transmitted
                    Pres Truman and Dept giving consideration means by which Korean interests
                    connection Japanese peace settlement can best be given expression. Not clear
                    from urtel whether intended message also to be sent to Dept to Prime Minister
                    Attlee Generalissimo CKS. Dept has taken no action this matter but raises
                    question whether messages might not be transmitted by Legislature or by USAFIK
                    acting for Legislature through Chinese and British Consuls Seoul. Your comment
                        requested.<anchor n="47" xml:id="d416-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d416-f1" n="47" xml:id="d416-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram 344, September 13, from Seoul, stated that the messages had already been
                    transmitted through the Consuls and that this procedure would be followed in
                    future cases (740.0011 PW (Peace)/9–1347).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
